  "metadata": {
    "title": "The Packhorse Arch",
    "description": "A humpbacked stone bridge over a river, wide enough for the hay wagon. Two sandstone arches carry a short paved crown over the water, and the road climbs to it from each bank in one unbroken slope. The bridge has no separate approaches: the ramps are the hump, so the climb and the crossing are one piece. 39 bricks.\n\n## How it is built\n\nEach step is a group in the Editor, so you can select it, delete it or build it again yourself.\n\n1. **River**: two blue Slab 4x4s make a stream 4 wide.\n2. **Arches**: four Arches stand in the river, two side by side on each side of the road. Their middle jambs meet to make a pier in midstream, and the water runs under both arches.\n3. **Crown**: a paved Slab 4x4 lies across the tops of the arches, 4 by 4.\n4. **Parapets**: two wooden Fences along each side of the crown.\n5. **Plinths**: on each bank, two sandstone Slab 4x4s stacked against the arches, with a sandstone Plate 2x4 in front as a kerb.\n6. **Haunches**: on each plinth, two sandstone Brick 1x4s turned 90° (press **R**) stand side by side against the arches.\n7. **Upper ramps**: four Shallow Slopes on each haunch climb to the crown. On the east side they are turned 180° so they climb toward the bridge.\n8. **Lower ramps**: four more Shallow Slopes on each plinth lead up to the haunch. Together the two rows make a road four wide all the way over.\n9. **Rocks**: one Rock on each bank, beside the water.\n\n## Wide enough for the hay wagon\n\nThe hay wagon is about 2 long and 1.4 wide over its wheels, and it takes up a circle 1.6 across. The ramps are 4 wide, and between the fences the crown is 3.6 wide, which leaves 1 to spare on each side. Nothing crosses over the road.\n\nThe plinths are what let it drive over. They lift the lower ramp so it meets the upper ramp exactly, and the upper ramp meets the crown exactly, so there is no edge anywhere on the way up: a wagon is wide enough that even a small edge at the top of a slope can stop it. The kerb splits the climb onto the plinth into two small steps. Each ramp climbs 1 for every 2 along, and the fences are tall enough that a wagon can't drive off the crown into the river.\n\n## Bricks\n\n- River: 2 Slab 4x4\n- Arches: 4 Arch\n- Crown: 1 Slab 4x4\n- Parapets: 4 Fence\n- Plinths: 4 Slab 4x4, 2 Plate 2x4\n- Haunches: 4 Brick 1x4\n- Upper ramps: 8 Shallow Slope 2x1\n- Lower ramps: 8 Shallow Slope 2x1\n- Rocks: 2 Rock\n\n39 bricks in all.",
